가 오른쪽으로 스와피프 되면서 수정할 수 있도록 변경해줘." (Change edit from double-click popup to edit icon in Grid, sliding window from right)\n\n10. **My implementation**: \n    - Replaced CrudDialog with Material-UI Drawer\n    - Added Actions column with Edit icon\n    - Removed double-click edit functionality\n    - Implemented slide-in panel from right\n\n11. **User's sixth request**: "나머지 페이지도 users 와 동일한 형태로 수정하는 방식을 일괄 수정해 줘." (Update remaining pages to match Users page format)\n\n12. **My implementation**: \n    - Updated Menus page with drawer and state persistence\n    - Updated Roles page with drawer and state persistence\n    - Updated Programs page with drawer and state persistence\n\n13. **User's final request**: "서비스를 중지하고 변경사항을 정리하여 git push 하라. 서비스는 내가 별도로 구동하겠다." (Stop services and organize changes for git push. User will start services separately)\n\n14. **My action**: Started checking for running Node processes but was interrupted by summary request.\n\nKey technical patterns:\n- SessionStorage for state persistence\n- Material-UI Drawer for slide-in panels\n- Centralized configuration management\n- Helper functions for URL management\n- Consistent UI patterns across all admin pages\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe user requested a comprehensive overhaul of the admin management pages in a Next.js enterprise application with the following specific requirements:\n\n1. **Avatar Image Implementation**: Add avatar/profile picture functionality to user management, displaying avatars when they exist and falling back to initials otherwise\n2. **Centralized Configuration**: Remove hardcoded backend URLs and implement centralized configuration management for better maintainability\n3. **State Persistence**: Preserve user's work (search criteria, pagination, results) when navigating between pages\n4. **UI/UX Modernization**: Replace double-click popup editing with a modern slide-in drawer interface triggered by edit icons\n5. **Consistency Across Pages**: Apply all improvements uniformly to all admin pages (Users, Menus, Roles, Programs)\n6. **Git Management**: Stop services and commit all changes to git\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **Next.js 14** with App Router and TypeScript\n- **Material-UI (MUI)** components and Drawer component\n- **SessionStorage API** for client-side state persistence\n- **Environment Variables** (.env files) for configuration management\n- **Multer** for file upload handling on backend\n- **Express.js** backend API routes\n- **bcrypt** for password hashing\n- **JWT** authentication with refresh tokens\n- **Axios** for API calls with interceptors\n- **React Hooks** (useState, useEffect, useMemo, useCallback)\n- **React Context API** for authentication state\n- **DataGrid** component customization\n- **File upload validation** (type, size)\n- **Responsive design** patterns\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n### Backend Files\n\n#### `backend/routes/user.js`\n- **Importance**: Main user API endpoints that needed avatarUrl field support\n- **Changes**: Added avatarUrl field handling in POST, PUT, and profile update endpoints\n```javascript\n// Line 216 - Added avatarUrl to request body destructuring\nconst { username, password, name, email, role, department, status, avatarUrl } = req.body;\n\n// Line 251 - Added avatarUrl to new user object\n...(avatarUrl && { avatarUrl })\n\n// Line 299 - Added avatarUrl update logic\nif (avatarUrl !== undefined) users[userIndex].avatarUrl = avatarUrl;\n\n// Line 492 - Added avatarUrl in profile update\nif (avatarUrl !== undefined) users[userIndex].avatarUrl = avatarUrl;\n```\n\n### Frontend Configuration Files\n\n#### `.env`\n- **Importance**: Development environment configuration\n- **Changes**: Added NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL\n```env\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api\nNEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3001\n```\n\n#### `.env.example`\n- **Importance**: Template for environment variables\n- **Changes**: Added NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL configuration example\n```env\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api\nNEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3001\n```\n\n#### `.env.production`\n- **Importance**: Production environment configuration\n- **Changes**: Added NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL (empty for same-domain deployment)\n```env\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api\nNEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=\n```\n\n#### `src/lib/config/index.ts` (NEW FILE)\n- **Importance**: Centralized configuration management for all URLs and settings\n- **Changes**: Created new file with helper functions and configuration constants\n```typescript\nexport const API_CONFIG = {\n  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3001/api',\n  backendURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL || 'http://localhost:3001',\n  timeout: 30000,\n} as const;\n\nexport const FILE_CONFIG = {\n  maxFileSize: 10 * 1024 * 1024,\n  allowedImageTypes: ['image/jpeg', 'image/jpg', 'image/png', 'image/gif', 'image/webp'],\n  uploadPath: '/uploads',\n} as const;\n\nexport function getAvatarUrl(avatarUrl: string | undefined | null): string | undefined {\n  if (!avatarUrl) return undefined;\n  if (avatarUrl.startsWith('http://') || avatarUrl.startsWith('https://')) {\n    return avatarUrl;\n  }\n  return `${API_CONFIG.backendURL}${avatarUrl}`;\n}\n\nexport function getFileUrl(filePath: string | undefined | null): string | undefined {\n  if (!filePath) return undefined;\n  if (filePath.startsWith('http://') || filePath.startsWith('https://')) {\n    return filePath;\n  }\n  return `${API_CONFIG.backendURL}${filePath}`;\n}\n```\n\n### TypeScript Type Definitions\n\n#### `src/types/auth.ts`\n- **Importance**: Core authentication types used throughout the application\n- **Changes**: Added avatarUrl field to User interface\n```typescript\nexport interface User {\n  id: string;\n  username: string;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  role: 'admin' | 'manager' | 'user';\n  department: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string; // NEW FIELD\n}\n```\n\n### Context and State Management\n\n#### `src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Global authentication state management\n- **Changes**: Added updateUser function to update user info after profile changes\n```typescript\ninterface AuthContextType extends AuthState {\n  login: (username: string, password=<REDACTED> => Promise<any>;\n  verifyMFA: (userId: string, code: string) => Promise<void>;\n  logout: () => Promise<void>;\n  refreshAccessToken: () => Promise<void>;\n  ssoLogin: () => Promise<void>;\n  updateUser: (user: any) => void; // NEW FUNCTION\n}\n\nconst updateUser = useCallback((updatedUser: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem('user', JSON.stringify(updatedUser));\n  setAuthState((prev) => ({\n    ...prev,\n    user: updatedUser\n  }));\n}, []);\n```\n\n### Component Files\n\n#### `src/components/layout/DashboardHeader/index.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Main application header showing user avatar\n- **Changes**: Updated Avatar component to use getAvatarUrl() helper\n```typescript\nimport { getAvatarUrl } from '@/lib/config';\n\n<Avatar\n  src={getAvatarUrl(user?.avatarUrl)}\n  alt={user?.name}\n  sx={{\n    width: 32,\n    height: 32,\n    bgcolor: 'secondary.main',\n    fontSize: '0.875rem',\n    fontWeight: 600\n  }}\n>\n  {!user?.avatarUrl && getUserInitials()}\n</Avatar>\n```\n\n#### `src/app/[locale]/dashboard/settings/page.tsx`\n- **Importance**: User settings page for profile management\n- **Changes**: Added avatar upload section with validation\n```typescript\nconst handleAvatarUpload = async (event: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n  const file = event.target.files?.[0];\n  if (!file) return;\n\n  const validTypes = ['image/jpeg', 'image/jpg', 'image/png', 'image/gif', 'image/webp'];\n  if (!validTypes.includes(file.type)) {\n    toast.error(locale === 'ko' ? '지원하지 않는 파일 형식입니다' : 'Unsupported file type');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (file.size > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {\n    toast.error(locale === 'ko' ? '파일 크기는 10MB를 초과할 수 없습니다' : 'File size cannot exceed 10MB');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const formData = new FormData();\n  formData.append('file', file);\n\n  setUploadingAvatar(true);\n  try {\n    const response = await api.post('/file/upload', formData, {\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data' },\n    });\n    const avatarUrl = response.file.path;\n    setProfileData({ ...profileData, avatarUrl });\n    toast.success(locale === 'ko' ? '아바타가 업로드되었습니다' : 'Avatar uploaded successfully');\n  } catch (error: unknown) {\n    const err = error as { response?: { data?: { error?: string } } };\n    toast.error(err.response?.data?.error || 'Failed to upload avatar');\n  } finally {\n    setUploadingAvatar(false);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### Admin Management Pages\n\n#### `src/app/[locale]/admin/users/page.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Main user management page - serves as template for other admin pages\n- **Major Changes**: \n  1. Added state persistence with sessionStorage\n  2. Replaced CrudDialog with Material-UI Drawer\n  3. Added Actions column with Edit icon\n  4. Removed double-click edit functionality\n\n**State Persistence Implementation**:\n```typescript\nconst STORAGE_KEY = 'admin-users-page-state';\n\nconst savePageState = (state: {\n  searchCriteria: SearchCriteria;\n  paginationModel: { page: number; pageSize: number };\n  quickSearch: string;\n  users: User[];\n  rowCount: number;\n}) => {\n  try {\n    sessionStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(state));\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to save page state:', error);\n  }\n};\n\nconst loadPageState = () => {\n  try {\n    const saved = sessionStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);\n    return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : null;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Failed to load page state:', error);\n    return null;\n  }\n};\n\n// Load saved state on mount\nconst savedState = loadPageState();\nconst [users, setUsers] = useState<User[]>(savedState?.users || []);\nconst [quickSearch, setQuickSearch] = useState(savedState?.quickSearch || '');\n\n// Auto-save state on changes\nuseEffect(() => {\n  savePageState({\n    searchCriteria,\n    paginationModel,\n    quickSearch,\n    users,\n    rowCount\n  });\n}, [searchCriteria, paginationModel, quickSearch, users, rowCount]);\n```\n\n**Actions Column Addition**:\n```typescript\nconst columns: GridColDef[] = [\n  // ... other columns\n  {\n    field: 'actions',\n    headerName: 'Actions',\n    width: 80,\n    sortable: false,\n    filterable: false,\n    renderCell: (params) => (\n      <IconButton\n        size="small"\n        onClick={() => handleEdit(params.row.id)}\n        color="primary"\n      >\n        <Edit fontSize="small" />\n      </IconButton>\n    )\n  }\n];\n```\n\n**Drawer Implementation**:\n```typescript\n<Drawer\n  anchor="right"\n  open={dialogOpen}\n  onClose={() => {\n    setDialogOpen(false);\n    setEditingUser(null);\n  }}\n  PaperProps={{\n    sx: { width: { xs: '100%', sm: 500 } }\n  }}\n>\n  <Box sx={{ height: '100%', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>\n    {/* Header */}\n    <Box sx={{\n      p: 2,\n      display: 'flex',\n      alignItems: 'center',\n      justifyContent: 'space-between',\n      borderBottom: 1,\n      borderColor: 'divider'\n    }}>\n      <Typography variant="h6">\n        {!editingUser?.id ? 'Add New User' : 'Edit User'}\n      </Typography>\n      <IconButton onClick={() => { setDialogOpen(false); setEditingUser(null); }}>\n        <Close />\n      </IconButton>\n    </Box>\n\n    {/* Form Content - Scrollable */}\n    <Box sx={{ flex: 1, overflow: 'auto', p: 3 }}>\n      <Stack spacing={3}>\n        {/* Avatar Upload */}\n        {/* Username Field */}\n        {/* Password Field (new users only) */}\n        {/* Name, Email, Role, Department, Status fields */}\n      </Stack>\n    </Box>\n\n    {/* Footer Actions */}\n    <Box sx={{\n      p: 2,\n      display: 'flex',\n      gap: 2,\n      justifyContent: 'flex-end',\n      borderBottom: 1,\n      borderColor: 'divider'\n    }}>\n      <Button variant="outlined" onClick={() => { /* close */ }}>\n        {t('common.cancel')}\n      </Button>\n      <Button variant="contained" onClick={handleSave} disabled={saveLoading}>\n        {saveLoading ? <CircularProgress size={20} /> : t('common.save')}\n      </Button>\n    </Box>\n  </Box>\n</Drawer>\n```\n\n**Removed DataGrid Props**:\n```typescript\n// REMOVED: editable, onEdit\n<ExcelDataGrid\n  rows={users}\n  columns={columns}\n  onRowsChange={(rows) => setUsers(rows as User[])}\n  onAdd={handleAdd}\n  onDelete={handleDeleteClick}\n  onRefresh={handleRefresh}\n  checkboxSelection\n  exportFileName="users"\n  loading={searching}\n  paginationMode="server"\n  rowCount={rowCount}\n  paginationModel={paginationModel}\n  onPaginationModelChange={handlePaginationModelChange}\n/>\n```\n\n#### `src/app/[locale]/admin/menus/page.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Menu management page\n- **Changes**: Applied same pattern as Users page (268 lines added, 106 removed, +162 net)\n- Includes menu-specific fields: Menu Code, Names (EN/KO), Path, Icon dropdown, Order, Level, Parent Menu, Program ID, Descriptions\n\n#### `src/app/[locale]/admin/roles/page.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Role management page\n- **Changes**: Applied same pattern with UserSelector components for Manager and Representative selection\n- Storage key: `'admin-roles-page-state'`\n\n#### `src/app/[locale]/admin/programs/page.tsx`\n- **Importance**: Program management page\n- **Changes**: Applied same pattern with Category, Type, Status dropdowns\n- Storage key: `'admin-programs-page-state'`\n- Includes fields: Program Code, Names (EN/KO), Category, Type, Status, Version, Author, Descriptions, Tags\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\n\n### Error 1: Unused imports after refactoring\n- **Description**: ESLint warnings about unused imports (CrudDialog, FormFieldConfig, API_CONFIG, etc.)\n- **Fix**: Removed unused imports and ran `npx eslint --fix` to clean up\n- **User Feedback**: None - proactively fixed\n\n### Error 2: Large JSON file reading\n- **Description**: users.json file (12.1MB) exceeded maximum read size\n- **Fix**: Used offset and limit parameters to read specific portions, then modified backend API routes instead of directly editing the large file\n- **User Feedback**: None - handled automatically\n\n### Error 3: Hardcoded URLs in multiple locations\n- **Description**: Backend URLs hardcoded as `http://localhost:3001` in multiple components\n- **Fix**: Created centralized config with `getAvatarUrl()` helper function and environment variables\n- **User Feedback**: User explicitly requested: "@src\\app\\[locale]\\admin\\users\\page.tsx backend 호출 주소가 고정되어 있어 운영에 어려움이 예상된다. 모든 설정은 한쪽으로 관리할 수 있도록 하여 유지보수성을 향상하라."\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n\n### Problem 1: State Loss on Navigation\n**Issue**: Users lose their search criteria and results when navigating away from admin pages and returning.\n\n**Solution**: Implemented sessionStorage-based persistence:\n- Save state automatically on changes using useEffect\n- Load state on component mount\n- Clear state when user explicitly clears search\n- Each page has unique storage key to prevent conflicts\n\n### Problem 2: Poor Mobile UX with Dialog\n**Issue**: CrudDialog not responsive, takes full screen on mobile, hard to dismiss\n\n**Solution**: Replaced with Material-UI Drawer:\n- Responsive width: `{ xs: '100%', sm: 500 }`\n- Slides in from right with animation\n- Easy to dismiss by clicking outside or X button\n- Fixed header and footer, scrollable content\n\n### Problem 3: Unclear Edit Action\n**Issue**: Double-click to edit is not discoverable, users may not know how to edit\n\n**Solution**: Added explicit Actions column with Edit icon:\n- Clear visual indicator\n- Removed ambiguous double-click behavior\n- Consistent with modern UI patterns\n\n### Problem 4: Centralized Configuration\n**Issue**: Backend URLs hardcoded in multiple places, difficult to maintain and deploy\n\n**Solution**: Created centralized configuration system:\n- Environment variables for different environments\n- Helper functions to construct URLs\n- Single source of truth for all API configurations\n- Easy to switch between dev/staging/production\n\n## 6. All User Messages\n\n1. "사용자관리" (User Management)\n2. "사용자관리에 Avatar 이미지를 추가하로 로그인시 아바타가 존재하면 아바타 이미지를 보여 주고 없다면 지금처럼." (Add Avatar image to user management, show avatar if exists during login, otherwise show as is)\n3. "@src\\app\\[locale]\\admin\\users\\page.tsx backend 호출 주소가 고정되어 있어 운영에 어려움이 예상된다. 모든 설정은 한쪽으로 관리할 수 있도록 하여 유지보수성을 향상하라." (Backend URLs are hardcoded causing operational difficulties. Improve maintainability by centralizing all configurations)\n4. "사용자관리에서 다른 메뉴로 이동하였다가 다시 사용자관리로 돌아오면 내용이 Reset 되어 있다. 작업내용을 저장할 수 있는가?" (When navigating away from user management and returning, content is reset. Can work be saved?)\n5. "사용자의 상세내용을 수정할 때 지금은 row를 더블클릭하여 팝업을 띄워 수정한다. 수정아이콘을 Grid 맨뒤에 넣고 클릭시 Windows가 오른쪽으로 스와피프 되면서 수정할 수 있도록 변경해줘." (Change edit from double-click popup to edit icon in Grid, sliding window from right)\n6. "나머지 페이지도 users 와 동일한 형태로 수정하는 방식을 일괄 수정해 줘." (Update remaining pages to match Users page format)\n7. "서비스를 중지하고 변경사항을 정리하여 git push 하라. 서비스는 내가 별도로 구동하겠다." (Stop services and organize changes for git push. User will start services separately)\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n1. **Stop running Node.js services** - Checked running processes (found 3 Node processes) but not yet stopped\n2. **Commit changes to Git** - Need to stage all changes and create meaningful commit message\n3. **Push to remote repository** - After committing, push to origin\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nImmediately before the summary request, I was working on **stopping services and preparing for Git commit** as requested by the user in their final message: "서비스를 중지하고 변경사항을 정리하여 git push 하라."\n\nI had just executed:\n```bash\ntasklist | findstr "node"\n```\n\nWhich returned:\n```\nnode.exe                     33412 Console                    7     46,028 K\nnode.exe                     25768 Console  