36c204d9-6931-46ad-9891-efcaf2e903ff	7a439db0-eb45-45b6-8bd5-0e05b23883ab	assistant	Perfect! Both frontend and backend are running. I've successfully fixed the 404 errors. Here's what was wrong and what I fixed:\n\n## Fixed Issues:\n\n### 1. **Incorrect API Endpoints in Frontend Hook** ([useProgramManagement.ts](src/app/[locale]/admin/programs/hooks/useProgramManagement.ts))\n\n**Problem:**\n- **Update (PUT)**: Used `/program` with id in request body instead of `/program/:id`\n- **Delete**: Used `/program?id=${id}` instead of `/program/${id}`\n\n**Fixed:**\n- Line 273: Changed `api.put('/program', { id: programData.id, ...apiData })` → `api.put(\\`/program/${programData.id}\\`, apiData)`\n- Line 226: Changed `api.delete(\\`/program?id=${id}\\`)` → `api.delete(\\`/program/${id}\\`)`\n\n### 2. **Inconsistent Data Format** ([backend/data/programs.json](backend/data/programs.json))\n\n**Problem:**\n- The last program entry (prog-014) used flat fields (`nameEn`, `nameKo`) instead of nested structure (`name.en`, `name.ko`)\n- This caused filtering to fail in the backend\n\n**Fixed:**\n- Converted prog-014 to use the correct nested format matching all other programs\n- Added proper structure with `name`, `description`, `permissions`, and `metadata` fields\n\n## Summary\n\nThe backend routes were correctly configured all along. The 404 errors were caused by the frontend calling wrong endpoint URLs. With these fixes, the Programs management page should now work correctly for:\n- ✅ Searching/filtering programs\n- ✅ Creating new programs  \n- ✅ Updating existing programs\n- ✅ Deleting programs\n\nThe application is ready to test. You can now access the Programs management page and it should load and operate without 404 errors.	text	\N	280	f	f	\N	\N	2025-11-09 14:58:32.292+00
