t menus to `menus.json` as children of menu-008 (Components menu)\n\n7. **Charts Component Request**: User asked to make charts reusable as common components. I discovered that Charts components already exist at `src/components/common/Charts/` with all necessary chart types already implemented (LineChart, BarChart, PieChart, AreaChart, ComposedChart, DonutChart, RadarChart).\n\n8. **Final Request**: User asked to create more complex, practical chart components for real-world applications.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**:\n   - Fix 404 error with `/menu/by-path` API endpoint (debugging added but not fully resolved)\n   - Fix runtime TypeError issues with all Picker components where `.format()` and `.includes()` methods were called on non-function values\n   - Systematically correct type mismatches between Picker components (which expect strings) and their demo pages (which were using Dayjs objects)\n   - Register all component demo pages under `/dev/components` as programs and menus in the backend JSON files\n   - Make chart components reusable as common components (discovered they already exist)\n   - Create additional complex, practical chart components for real-world applications\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts**:\n   - Next.js 16.0.1 with TypeScript and App Router\n   - Material-UI (MUI) v6 with @mui/x-date-pickers\n   - Day.js for date/time manipulation with various plugins (localizedFormat, quarterOfYear, isLeapYear, relativeTime, dayOfYear, weekOfYear)\n   - Express.js backend on port 3001\n   - Axios for HTTP requests with interceptors\n   - Type safety issues between component interfaces and usage\n   - String-based date/time values vs Dayjs objects\n   - React hooks (useState, useCallback, useEffect)\n   - Recharts 3.3.0 for data visualization\n   - Menu and program permission system with JSON-based configuration\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections**:\n\n   **Backend Files Modified:**\n   \n   - `backend/middleware/logger.js` (lines 56-69)\n     - Added `url` and `originalUrl` fields for better debugging of 404 errors\n     ```javascript\n     const logEntry = {\n       id: uuidv4(),\n       timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n       method: req.method,\n       path: req.path,\n       url: req.url,  // ADDED\n       originalUrl: req.originalUrl,  // ADDED\n       statusCode: res.statusCode,\n       duration: `${duration}ms`,\n       userId: req.user?.userId || 'anonymous',\n       programId: getProgramIdFromPath(req.path),\n       ip: req.ip || req.connection.remoteAddress,\n       userAgent: req.headers['user-agent']\n     };\n     ```\n\n   - `backend/data/programs.json`\n     - Added 27 new component demo programs (prog-comp-001 through prog-comp-027)\n     - Each program has category "component", type "demo", status "active"\n     - All have READ permission with isDefault: true\n     - Programs include: DataGrid, Empty State, Page Header, Rich Text Editor, File Upload, Date Range Picker, Date Picker, Year Picker, Month Picker, Time Picker, DateTime Picker, DateTime Range Picker, Multi Select, Avatar Upload, User Selector, Quick Search, Search Filter, Advanced Search, User Search, CRUD Dialog, Edit Drawer, Delete Confirm, Help Viewer, Page Container, Actions Cell, Status Menu, Charts\n\n   - `backend/data/menus.json`\n     - Added 27 new submenu items (menu-comp-001 through menu-comp-027)\n     - All are children of menu-008 (Components menu) with level 2\n     - Each menu has appropriate Material-UI icon, order, programId, and descriptions in English and Korean\n\n   **Frontend Axios Configuration:**\n   \n   - `src/lib/axios/index.ts` (lines 15-38)\n     - Added debug logging to request interceptor\n     ```typescript\n     axiosInstance.interceptors.request.use(\n       (config) => {\n         if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\n           const token = localStorage.getItem('accessToken');\n           if (token) {\n             config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;\n           }\n         }\n         // Debug logging - ADDED\n         console.log('[Axios Request]', {\n           url: config.url,\n           baseURL: config.baseURL,\n           fullURL: `${config.baseURL}${config.url}`,\n           params: config.params\n         });\n         return config;\n       },\n       // ...\n     );\n     ```\n\n   **Picker Demo Pages Fixed:**\n   \n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/time-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''`, `'09:00:00'`, `dayjs().format('HH:mm:ss')`\n     - Display changed from `time1.format('HH:mm:ss')` to `time1`\n     ```typescript\n     const [time1, setTime1] = useState<string>('');\n     const [time2, setTime2] = useState<string>('09:00:00');\n     const [time3, setTime3] = useState<string>(dayjs().format('HH:mm:ss'));\n     ```\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/date-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''`, `dayjs().format('YYYY-MM-DD') + 'T00:00:00'`\n     - Display changed from `date1.format(...)` to `date1.split('T')[0]` and `dayjs(date1).format(...)`\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/year-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''`, `dayjs().format('YYYY')`, `'2020'`\n     - Display changed from `year1.format('YYYY')` to `year1`\n     - Used `parseInt(year2)` for numeric calculations\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/month-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''`, `dayjs().format('YYYY-MM')`, `dayjs().subtract(1, 'month').format('YYYY-MM')`\n     - Display changed from `month1.format('YYYY-MM')` to `month1`\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/datetime-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''`, `dayjs().format('YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss')`, `''`\n     - Display changed from `dateTime1.format(...)` to `dateTime1.replace('T', ' ')`\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/datetime-range-picker/page.tsx`\n     - Changed from: `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>`\n     - Initial values: `''` for both start and end, and `dayjs().startOf('day').format('YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss')` / `dayjs().endOf('day').format('YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss')`\n     - Fixed prop usage from non-existent `onStartChange` and `onEndChange` to correct `onChange` callback:\n     ```typescript\n     <DateTimeRangePicker\n       startDateTime={startDateTime}\n       endDateTime={endDateTime}\n       onChange={(start, end) => {\n         setStartDateTime(start);\n         setEndDateTime(end);\n       }}\n       startLabel="Start Date & Time"\n       endLabel="End Date & Time"\n     />\n     ```\n\n   **Chart Components Reviewed:**\n   \n   - `src/components/common/Charts/index.ts`\n     - Exports all chart components: LineChart, BarChart, PieChart, AreaChart, ComposedChart, DonutChart, RadarChart\n     - All components already implemented with TypeScript types\n\n   - `src/components/common/Charts/LineChart.tsx`\n     - Full-featured line chart with Material-UI theming\n     - Custom tooltip component\n     - Support for curved/linear lines, multiple series, grid, legend\n     - Props include data, series, height, showGrid, showLegend, showTooltip, xAxisLabel, yAxisLabel, paper, curved\n\n   - `src/components/common/Charts/BarChart.tsx`\n     - Support for horizontal/vertical orientation\n     - Stacked bars support via stackId\n     - Custom tooltip with Material-UI styling\n     - Props include horizontal, barSize, and all common chart props\n\n   - `src/app/[locale]/dev/components/charts/page.tsx`\n     - Comprehensive demo page showing all chart types\n     - Sample data for each chart type\n     - Code examples and API reference\n     - Already using the common chart components from `@/components/common/Charts`\n\n4. **Errors and Fixes**:\n\n   - **Error 1**: `timeStr.includes is not a function` in TimePicker\n     - **Cause**: Demo page passed `Dayjs` object where `string` was expected\n     - **Fix**: Changed `useState<Dayjs | null>` to `useState<string>` and updated all related code to use formatted strings\n\n   - **Error 2**: `date1.format is not a function` in DatePicker\n     - **Cause**: Same type mismatch - Dayjs object instead of string\n     - **Fix**: Updated state type and all display logic to work with strings, used `dayjs(date1).format()` pattern when needed\n\n   - **Error 3**: `year1.format is not a function` in YearPicker\n     - **Cause**: Same type mismatch\n     - **Fix**: Updated state type, used `parseInt()` for year calculations instead of Dayjs methods\n\n   - **Error 4**: `month1.format is not a function` in MonthPicker\n     - **Cause**: Same type mismatch\n     - **Fix**: Updated state type, used `dayjs(month3).format()` pattern for display transformations\n\n   - **Error 5**: `dateTime1.format is not a function` in DateTimePicker\n     - **Cause**: Same type mismatch\n     - **Fix**: Updated state type, used `.replace('T', ' ')` for display formatting\n\n   - **Error 6**: `onChange is not a function` in DateTimeRangePicker\n     - **Cause**: Demo page used non-existent props `onStartChange` and `onEndChange` instead of the correct `onChange` prop\n     - **Component signature**: `onChange: (startDateTime: string, endDateTime: string) => void`\n     - **Fix**: Updated demo page to use correct `onChange` prop with a callback that receives both start and end values, then sets them individually\n\n5. **Problem Solving**:\n   - Identified systematic type mismatch pattern across all Picker components\n   - Components consistently use `string` types for date/time values in specific formats:\n     - TimePicker: HH:mm:ss\n     - DatePicker: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss (but displayed as YYYY-MM-DD)\n     - YearPicker: YYYY\n     - MonthPicker: YYYY-MM\n     - DateTimePicker: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss\n     - DateTimeRangePicker: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss for both start and end\n   - Solution pattern: Convert state to `string`, format initial values appropriately, update display logic to work with strings or wrap in `dayjs()` when needed\n   - Successfully registered 27 component demo programs and menus\n   - Discovered existing comprehensive Chart component library already in place\n\n6. **All User Messages**:\n   - "아래 오류의 원인을 파악하고 해결해 줘." (404 error with `/menu/by-path`)\n   - "아래 오류를 분석하여 해결해 줘." (TimePicker `timeStr.includes is not a function`)\n   - "아래 오류를 해결해 줘." (DatePicker `date1.format is not a function`)\n   - "아래 오류를 해결해 줘." (YearPicker `year1.format is not a function`)\n   - "아래 오류를 수정해 줘." (MonthPicker `month1.format is not a function`)\n   - "아래 오류를 수정해 줘." (DateTimePicker `dateTime1.format is not a function`)\n   - "아래 문제를 해결해 줘." (DateTimeRangePicker `onChange is not a function`)\n   - "src\\app\\[locale]\\dev 이하 React 학습을 위한 페이지를 작성한다. 관련 프로그램과 메뉴를 등록 해 줘."\n   - "@src\\app\\[locale]\\dev\\components\\charts\\page.tsx 그래프를 재활용할 수 있도록 각 종류별 공토 컴포넌트로 만들어 줘."\n   - "조금더 복합적이고 실제 응용이 잘 되는 차트를 추가로 공통컴포넌트로 만들어 줘."\n\n7. **Pending Tasks**:\n   - Create additional complex, practical chart components for real-world applications (currently in progress)\n   - Tasks identified: StackedAreaChart, MixedBarLineChart, MultiAxisChart, TrendChart components\n   - Potentially investigate and resolve the original 404 error with `/menu/by-path` (debugging was added but resolution not confirmed)\n\n8. **Current Work**:\n   Just before the summary request, I was about to create additional complex chart components for real-world applications. The user's exact request was: "조금더 복합적이고 실제 응용이 잘 되는 차트를 추가로 공통컴포넌트로 만들어 줘."\n\n   I had:\n   - Created a todo list with pending tasks: StackedAreaChart, MixedBarLineChart, MultiAxisChart, TrendChart components\n   - Verified that Recharts 3.3.0 is installed\n   - Discovered that basic chart components already exist at `src