6b4796a3-81ad-410f-af27-b649835eaa15	a3615b2a-154a-4650-8eaa-edb09172fd08	user	This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The conversation is summarized below:\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze the conversation:\n\n1. **Initial Request**: User asked to check the current state of the mail system upgrade.\n   - I checked the mail tables, migrations, and confirmed v2 schema is in place\n   - Found 3 core tables: mail_messages, mail_recipients, mail_user_messages\n   - Backend routes and services are complete\n   - Frontend pages exist in src/app/[locale]/mail/\n\n2. **Second Request**: User said to proceed with remaining work (excluding external mail testing):\n   - Clean up old mail tables\n   - Verify attachment functionality\n   - Test with test data\n   \n3. **Old Tables Cleanup**: Dropped unused tables:\n   - mail_attachments, mail_folders, mail_labels, mail_message_labels, mail_queue, mail_settings\n\n4. **Attachment Integration**: \n   - Added file upload UI to compose page\n   - Added attachment states and handlers\n   - Added i18n translations for mail\n\n5. **TypeScript Errors Fixed**:\n   - Duplicate `mail` key in i18n files - merged keys into existing mail section\n   - `recipient_name`/`recipient_email` not in MailMessage type - created getRecipientDisplay helper function\n\n6. **Test Data**: Created 3 test mail messages with recipients and user_messages\n\n7. **Git Operations**: User wanted to force merge after sensitive data removal caused conflicts\n   - Branch protection prevented force push\n   - User manually disabled protection and pushed\n\n8. **Continue Mail Work**: User asked to continue mail work\n\n9. **MultiUserSelect Component**: User requested modern UI/UX for recipient input\n   - Created new `MultiUserSelect.tsx` component with Gmail/Outlook style\n   - Multiple recipients with chips inside input field\n   - Avatar initials, search functionality\n\n10. **Common Components Usage**: User asked to use common components where possible\n   - Checked available components: AttachmentUpload, PageHeader, Card, etc.\n   - Started replacing manual file upload with AttachmentUpload component\n   - In progress when summary was requested\n\nCurrent work in progress:\n- Replacing manual attachment code with AttachmentUpload common component\n- Already updated imports and removed manual file handlers\n- Need to update the UI section to use AttachmentUpload component\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Check and upgrade the mail system (v2 with multi-recipient support)\n   - Clean up old mail tables, verify attachment functionality, test with data\n   - Improve recipient input UI/UX using common components (Gmail/Outlook style)\n   - Force merge to main branch after git history rewrite for sensitive data removal\n   - Use common components wherever possible in mail compose page\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Mail System v2 with multi-recipient support (To/CC/BCC)\n   - PostgreSQL mail tables: mail_messages, mail_recipients, mail_user_messages\n   - Express.js backend routes/services for mail API\n   - Next.js frontend with StandardCrudPageLayout\n   - MUI Autocomplete with multiple selection for recipients\n   - AttachmentUpload common component with drag-and-drop\n   - Git force push with branch protection handling\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`src/components/common/MultiUserSelect.tsx`** (NEW)\n     - Modern Gmail-style multi-user selection component\n     - Chips inside input field, avatar initials, debounced search\n     ```typescript\n     export interface MultiUserSelectProps {\n       value: UserOption[];\n       onChange: (users: UserOption[]) => void;\n       label?: string;\n       placeholder?: string;\n       disabled?: boolean;\n       error?: boolean;\n       helperText?: string;\n       size?: 'small' | 'medium';\n       maxHeight?: number;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/app/[locale]/mail/compose/page.tsx`** (MODIFIED - IN PROGRESS)\n     - Updated imports to use MultiUserSelect and AttachmentUpload\n     - Changed recipient state from `Recipient[]` to `UserOption[]`\n     - Removed manual file upload handlers (handleFileUpload, handleFileDelete, formatFileSize)\n     - Changed `attachment` state to simple `attachmentId` string\n     ```typescript\n     // Current imports\n     import MultiUserSelect, { UserOption } from '@/components/common/MultiUserSelect';\n     import AttachmentUpload from '@/components/common/AttachmentUpload';\n     \n     // Current state\n     const [toRecipients, setToRecipients] = useState<UserOption[]>([]);\n     const [ccRecipients, setCcRecipients] = useState<UserOption[]>([]);\n     const [attachmentId, setAttachmentId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n     ```\n     - Still has OLD attachment UI code that needs replacement (lines 377-440)\n\n   - **`src/app/[locale]/mail/components/MailPageContent.tsx`** (MODIFIED)\n     - Added `getRecipientDisplay` helper to handle v2 recipients array\n     - Fixed TypeScript errors for missing recipient_name/recipient_email\n\n   - **`src/lib/i18n/locales/en.ts`** and **`ko.ts`** (MODIFIED)\n     - Added mail-related translations: attach, attachments, attachmentUploadFailed, etc.\n     - Fixed duplicate mail key issue by merging into existing section\n\n   - **`src/components/common/AttachmentUpload/index.tsx`** (READ)\n     - Existing component with drag-and-drop, progress tracking, file list\n     - Uses useAttachment hook, supports attachmentTypeCode\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Duplicate mail key in i18n**: Had two `mail:` sections in en.ts/ko.ts\n     - Fixed by merging new keys into existing mail section\n   - **recipient_name/recipient_email not in MailMessage type**: V2 uses recipients array\n     - Fixed by creating getRecipientDisplay() helper function\n   - **Git force push rejected**: Branch protection on main\n     - User manually disabled protection and pushed\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Cleaned