ities\n     - User service\n     - Auth service (login, MFA, refresh, logout, register)\n     - Auth middleware\n     - Rate limiters\n     - Routes\n   - Updated package.json with dependencies\n   - Created .env.example\n\n8. **Frontend Updates**:\n   - Modified axios configuration to support environment-based API routing\n   - Updated AuthContext to work with new Auth Service API format\n   - Added resendMFA function\n   - Handled both old and new API response formats\n\n9. **Type Errors Fixed**:\n   - Fixed `rowCount` null check in userService.ts\n   - Fixed jwt.sign expiresIn type in shared/utils/jwt.ts\n   - Fixed AuthenticatedRequest type in shared/types/api.ts\n   - Fixed getDatabase return type in shared/config/database.ts\n\nCurrent work was fixing TypeScript errors in the auth-service before the summary was requested.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - User requested review of monitoring tools (Prometheus, Grafana, etc.) and comparison of options\n   - User chose Prometheus + Grafana + Loki stack for implementation\n   - User requested port change for Prometheus (9090 → 9092) to avoid DB port conflict\n   - User requested summary of target architecture and progress\n   - User requested Phase 2 implementation: Auth Service migration including:\n     - Legacy Backend auth code analysis\n     - Auth Service API implementation (login, register, refresh, logout)\n     - Redis session store integration\n     - Frontend useAuth hook modification\n     - Integration testing\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MSA (Microservices Architecture) with 5 services + legacy backend\n   - Prometheus for metrics collection with alert rules\n   - Grafana for visualization with auto-provisioned dashboards\n   - Loki + Promtail for log aggregation\n   - JWT authentication with access/refresh tokens\n   - Redis for token blacklist and MFA code storage\n   - Rate limiting for auth endpoints\n   - PostgreSQL database (shared)\n   - Environment-based API routing (development: direct, production: via API Gateway)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Monitoring Configuration:**\n   - `infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.yml` - Added Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Promtail services; changed Prometheus port to 9092\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/prometheus/prometheus.yml` - Scrape configs for all services\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/prometheus/alert.rules.yml` - Alert rules for ServiceDown, HighErrorRate, etc.\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/loki/loki-config.yml` - Log storage configuration\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/promtail/promtail-config.yml` - Docker log collection\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/grafana/provisioning/datasources/datasources.yml` - Prometheus & Loki datasources\n   - `infrastructure/monitoring/grafana/dashboards/*.json` - 3 dashboards\n\n   **Auth Service Implementation:**\n   - `services/auth-service/package.json` - Added dependencies (pg, jsonwebtoken, bcryptjs, ioredis, express-rate-limit, uuid)\n   ```json\n   {\n     "dependencies": {\n       "@enterprise/shared": "file:../../shared",\n       "express": "^4.21.0",\n       "pg": "^8.11.0",\n       "jsonwebtoken": "^9.0.0",\n       "bcryptjs": "^2.4.3",\n       "ioredis": "^5.3.0",\n       "express-rate-limit": "^7.1.0",\n       "uuid": "^9.0.0"\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n   - `services/auth-service/src/types/index.ts` - User, LoginRequest, LoginResponse, TokenPayload types\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/utils/database.ts` - PostgreSQL connection pool\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/utils/redis.ts` - Redis utilities for blacklist, MFA codes, sessions\n   ```typescript\n   export const addToBlacklist = async (token: string, expiresInSeconds: number): Promise<void>\n   export const isBlacklisted = async (token: string): Promise<boolean>\n   export const storeMFACode = async (userId: string, code: string, expiresInSeconds: number): Promise<void>\n   export const verifyMFACode = async (userId: string, code: string): Promise<boolean>\n   ```\n\n   - `services/auth-service/src/utils/jwt.ts` - JWT generation and verification\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/utils/password.ts` - bcrypt hashing, MFA code generation\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/services/userService.ts` - User database operations\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/services/authService.ts` - Core auth logic (login, verifyMFA, resendMFA, refreshAccessToken, logout, register, validateToken)\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/middleware/authMiddleware.ts` - JWT authentication middleware\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/middleware/rateLimiter.ts` - Rate limiters (login: 5/min, MFA: 10/5min, register: 3/hour)\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/routes/auth.ts` - All auth endpoints\n   \n   - `services/auth-service/src/server.ts` - Express server with routes\n\n   **Frontend Updates:**\n   - `src/lib/axios/index.ts` - Added environment-based API URL selection, createServiceApi helper\n   \n   - `src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx` - Updated to work with new Auth Service:\n   ```typescript\n   const getAuthApiUrl = (): string => {\n     const config = getApiConfig();\n     const env = getEnvironment();\n     if (env === 'development') {\n       return config.auth; // Direct call to auth service\n     }\n     return ''; // Relative path via API Gateway\n   };\n   ```\n\n   **Shared Library Fixes:**\n   - `shared/utils/jwt.ts` - Fixed expiresIn type:\n   ```typescript\n   return jwt.sign(payload, JWT_SECRET, {\n     expiresIn: JWT_EXPIRES_IN as jwt.SignOptions['expiresIn'],\n   });\n   ```\n   \n   - `shared/types/api.ts` - Fixed AuthenticatedRequest type:\n   ```typescript\n   export interface AuthenticatedRequest extends Omit<Request, 'user'> {\n     user?: JwtPayload & { type?: string };\n   }\n   ```\n   \n   - `shared/config/database.ts` - Fixed getDatabase return with non-null assertion:\n   ```typescript\n   return dbInstance!;\n   ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Prometheus port conflict**: User noted DB uses port 9090, changed Prometheus to 9092\n   - **TypeScript error in userService.ts**: `result.rowCount` possibly null\n     - Fixed with: `return (result.rowCount ?? 0) > 0;`\n   - **TypeScript error in shared/utils/jwt.ts**: expiresIn type mismatch with jsonwebtoken v9\n     - Fixed with: `expiresIn: JWT_EXPIRES_IN as jwt.SignOptions['expiresIn']`\n   - **TypeScript error in shared/types/api.ts**: AuthenticatedRequest 'user' type incompatible\n     - Fixed with: `extends Omit<Request, 'user'>` and adding `& { type?: string }`\n   - **TypeScript error in shared/config/database.ts**: Return type null issue\n     - Fixed with: `return dbInstance!;`\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Designed monitoring architecture with Prometheus + Grafana + Loki\n   - Created comprehensive auth service that mirrors legacy backend functionality\n   - Handled API response format compatibility (both old `token` and new `accessToken` formats)\n   - Implemented environment-based API routing for development vs production\n   - Currently fixing TypeScript compilation errors in shared library\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - "초기 단계부터 prometheus 나 Grafana 와 같은 서비스 모니터링을 도구를 검토하고 장단점을 비교하라."\n   - "5. 최종 권장: Prometheus + Grafana + Loki 로 진행하라."\n   - "Prometheus 포트가 현재 DB 포트와 헷갈릴 수 있으니 다른 PORT를 사용하라."\n   - "지금까지 내용을 git에 commit 하라."\n   - "현재기준 목표 아키텍처와 현재까지 진행사항을 정리해 줘."\n   - "다음단계를 진행하라. Phase 2: Auth Service 분리 1. Legacy Backend에서 인증 관련 코드 분리 2. Auth Service에 API 구현 (login, register, refresh, logout) 3. Redis 세션 저장소 연동 4. Frontend useAuth 훅 수정 5. 통합 테스트"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete TypeScript error fixes in auth-service\n   - Integration testing of Auth Service\n   - Git commit for Phase 2 changes\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was fixing TypeScript compilation errors in the auth-service. After running `npx tsc --noEmit`, several errors were found:\n   - Fixed `rowCount` null check in userService.ts\n   - Fixed jwt.sign expiresIn type in shared/utils/jwt.ts  \n   - Fixed AuthenticatedRequest type in shared/types/api.ts\n   - Fixed getDatabase return type in shared/config/database.ts\n   \n   The last action was editing `shared/config/database.ts` to add non-null assertion to the return statement.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run TypeScript check again to verify all errors are fixed, then proceed with testing the auth-service:\n   ```bash\n   cd "E:/apps/nextjs-enterprise-app/services/auth-service" && npx tsc --noEmit\n   ```\n   \n   From the todo list:\n   - [in_progress] Auth Service 의존성 설치 및 테스트\n   - [pending] Git 커밋\n\n   The user's explicit request was: "다음단계를 진행하라. Phase 2: Auth Service 분리" with specific tasks including integration testing and git commit..\nPlease continue the conversation from where we left it off without asking the user any further questions. Continue with the last task that you were asked to work on.	text	\N	272	f	f	\N	\N	2025-12-08 14:05:51.169+00
