ring;\n       department?: string;\n       position?: string;\n       avatarUrl?: string;\n       employee_number?: string;\n       phone_number?: string;\n       mobile_number?: string;\n       permissions?: string[];\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`services/auth-service/.env`**\n     - Updated JWT secrets to match legacy backend\n     ```env\n     JWT_SECRET=<REDACTED>\n     JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=<REDACTED>\n     REDIS_ENABLED=false\n     ```\n\n   - **`infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.yml`**\n     - Updated to match existing docker/docker-compose.yml structure\n     - Uses external PostgreSQL (<REDACTED_IP>:9090)\n     - Added healthchecks for services\n     - Monitoring services moved to optional profile\n     - Removed APISIX/etcd (not needed for initial deployment)\n     - Commented out unimplemented services\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`.env` file indentation**: Environment variables had leading spaces, causing them to not load\n     - Fixed by removing indentation from `.env` file\n   \n   - **dotenv import order**: Database connection tried to use env vars before dotenv loaded\n     - Fixed by moving `import 'dotenv/config'` to top of server.ts\n   \n   - **DB column "name" does not exist**: DB uses `name_ko`, `name_en` instead of `name`\n     - User feedback: "코드를 새로 작성하지 말고 기존 backend 소스를 참조하여 구현하라"\n     - Fixed by updating SQL queries and types to match actual DB schema\n   \n   - **column rpm.program_id does not exist**: `getUserPermissions` query referenced non-existent table structure\n     - Fixed by removing the function entirely (not used in legacy backend)\n   \n   - **JWT invalid signature**: Auth Service and Legacy Backend used different JWT secrets\n     - Fixed by copying JWT secrets from `.env.local` to Auth Service's `.env`\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully implemented Redis In-Memory fallback for Docker-less development\n   - Matched Auth Service response format with legacy backend for compatibility\n   - Resolved JWT token shari