kage.json` - added @types/express\n- `services/auth-service/Dockerfile` - symlink fix\n\nThe most recent work was starting Phase 3: Admin Service creation. User explicitly said to proceed but reference existing backend code to avoid errors. I explored the backend admin-related routes and services comprehensively.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Continue MSA migration project, specifically Phase 3: Admin Service 분리\n   - Admin Service should handle: 사용자/역할/메뉴 관리 (User/Role/Menu management)\n   - User explicitly stated: "항상 진행 하되 기존 backend 서비스를 참고하여 오류가 발생하지 않도록 하라" (Always proceed but reference existing backend services to avoid errors)\n   - Previous work included deploying to server with Docker Compose, integrating APISIX (temporarily disabled due to issues)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MSA (Microservices Architecture) migration\n   - Docker Compose for container orchestration\n   - APISIX API Gateway (temporarily disabled)\n   - Nginx as reverse proxy (direct routing to services)\n   - TypeScript/Node.js services\n   - PostgreSQL external database (<REDACTED_IP>:9090)\n   - Redis for session/token management\n   - JWT authentication with shared secrets\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.yml`**\n     - Final state: APISIX commented out, direct routing via Nginx\n     - Key services: postgres, nginx, redis, frontend, backend, auth-service\n     ```yaml\n     # Nginx depends on backend now (APISIX disabled)\n     nginx:\n       depends_on:\n         backend:\n           condition: service_healthy\n         frontend:\n           condition: service_started\n     \n     # APISIX commented out\n     # apisix:\n     #   image: apache/apisix:3.8.0-debian\n     #   ...\n     ```\n\n   - **`infrastructure/nginx/nginx.conf`**\n     - Direct upstream to services (not via APISIX)\n     ```nginx\n     upstream backend {\n         server corenext-backend:3001;\n         keepalive 64;\n     }\n\n     upstream au